## Kindergarten incursions FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="What ages are your kindergarten incursions for?" %}
Our kindergarten incursions suit babies through to pre-prep. In addition, we adapt every activity to the children’s ages, abilities and developmental stages.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How long does a session run?" %}
Sessions run for 30 to 45 minutes, depending on the age group and your centre’s needs.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do we need to supply instruments?" %}
No. We bring African djembes and a variety of unique percussion instruments, so every child has one to play.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How do your incursions link to the EYLF?" %}
They support Belonging, Being and Becoming, as well as all five EYLF learning outcomes: identity, community, wellbeing, learning and communication.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Which areas do you visit?" %}
We visit early learning centres on the Sunshine Coast and in Brisbane, as well as across Australia. What’s more, there are no travel fees.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How much does a kindergarten incursion cost?" %}
Pricing depends on your group sizes and session times. So send us your centre, preferred date and number of children, and we’ll provide a quote.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
